  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ndpi_search_bittorrent_hash",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/bittorrent.c",
    "description": "The function unconditionally copies 20 payload-controlled bytes into `flow->protos.bittorrent.hash`. That hash shares a union with `flow->protos.tls_quic`, whose first members are heap pointers. For a combined TLS/BitTorrent flow, the copy therefore overwrites `tls_quic.server_names` and adjacent pointer state even though the structure explicitly says TLS/BitTorrent flows must not access the BitTorrent hash. When the flow is released, `ndpi_free_flow_data()` sees TLS in the protocol stack and passes the corrupted `server_names` value to `ndpi_free()`, causing the wild-address read in ASan's allocator.",
    "conditions": "A packet from the fuzzed PCAP must belong to a flow that retains TLS as one detected protocol and is also recognized as BitTorrent. Its payload must contain `BitTorrent protocol` in a recognized handshake position and provide at least 20 bytes after the computed hash offset, satisfying the length check in `ndpi_search_bittorrent_hash`. `ndpi_add_connection_as_bittorrent()` requests hash extraction before preserving the existing TLS master protocol; the payload bytes are copied over the TLS pointer fields. In this PoV, space bytes become a high invalid pointer (for example `0x2020202020202020`), and immediate completed-flow cleanup reaches `ndpi_free_flow_data()` and attempts to free it."
  },
